        "---\n",
        "#  Quick Reference: Preprocessing Cheat Sheet\n",
        "\n",
        "| Task | Code | When |\n",
        "|------|------|------|\n",
        "| Standard scaling | `StandardScaler().fit_transform(X)` | Most ML algorithms |\n",
        "| MinMax scaling | `MinMaxScaler().fit_transform(X)` | Neural networks |\n",
        "| Label encode | `df['col'].map({'a':0, 'b':1})` | Ordered categories |\n",
        "| One-hot encode | `pd.get_dummies(df, drop_first=True)` | Unordered categories |\n",
        "| Train/test split | `train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.2)` | Always |\n",
        "| Stratified split | `train_test_split(..., stratify=y)` | Imbalanced classes |\n",
        "| Correlation matrix | `df.corr()` | Feature selection |\n",
        "| Z-score outliers | `scipy.stats.zscore(col)` | Normal-ish data |\n",
        "| IQR outliers | `Q1 - 1.5*IQR` to `Q3 + 1.5*IQR` | Skewed data |\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Correct Order of Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Handle missing values (`fillna`, `dropna`)\n",
        "2. Feature engineering (create new columns)\n",
        "3. Encode categoricals (one-hot, label encoding)\n",
        "4. Remove outliers (z-score or IQR)\n",
        "5. **Train/Test split (MUST be before scaling!)**\n",
        "6. Scale features (`fit` on train, `transform` both)\n",
        "7. Feature selection (correlation, importance)\n",
        "\n",
        "> Scalers and encoders are fit ONLY on training data."
      ]
    },
