        "---\n",
        "# Assignment: Preprocess the Titanic Dataset End-to-End\n",
        "\n",
        "Apply everything from this session to the Titanic dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Dataset:** Titanic passengers  \n",
        "> **URL:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv`  \n",
        "> **Target variable:** Survived (0 = died, 1 = survived)  \n",
        "> **Goal:** Produce clean, scaled, split train/test sets ready for ML modelling\n",
        "\n",
        "## Task 1: Load and Initial Cleanup\n",
        "\n",
        "- Load the CSV\n",
        "- Drop columns: `PassengerId`, `Name`, `Ticket`, `Cabin`\n",
        "- Fill `Age` with median, `Embarked` with mode\n",
        "- Verify zero missing values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Load the CSV\n",
        "url = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv'\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Drop columns\n",
        "df = df.drop(columns=['PassengerId', 'Name', 'Ticket', 'Cabin'])\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Fill missing values\n",
        "df['Age'] = df['Age'].fillna(df['Age'].median())\n",
        "df['Embarked'] = df['Embarked'].fillna(df['Embarked'].mode()[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4. Verify zero missing values\n",
        "missing_counts = df.isnull().sum()\n",
        "print(\"Missing values per column:\")\n",
        "print(missing_counts)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nTotal missing values: {missing_counts.sum()}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "df.head()"
